.TH MAN 1 "30 October 2026" "amix-base"
.SH NAME
man \- display a manual page, from the add-on packages or from the stock system
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B man
[
.I section
]
.I name ...
.br
.B man \-k
.I keyword ...
.br
.B man \-f
.I name ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B man
shows the manual page for each
.IR name .
It looks first among the pages of the add-on packages, in
.BR /opt/amix/man ,
and when it finds none there it hands the request to the stock
.BR /usr/bin/man ,
which shows the system's own pages.
So one command reaches both, and a package's page wins over a stock page of
the same name (a GNU
.B grep
page over the stock one, for example).
To see the stock page in that case, run
.B /usr/bin/man
directly.
.PP
With a
.I section
(a section number such as 1 or 3, or the name of a section directory) only that
section is searched. Without one, the sections are tried in the order
1, 1m, 8, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, then any other.
.PP
A page is formatted with
.BR tbl ,
.BR eqn ,
.B nroff
.B \-man
and
.BR col ,
the same way the stock
.B man
formats a page, and shown through the pager named by
.BR PAGER ,
by default
.BR /usr/bin/more ,
when the output is a terminal.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-k " keyword"
List the pages whose index line contains
.IR keyword :
the packages' lines first, then the stock index.
.TP
.BI \-f " name"
List the index lines for the page
.IR name ,
in the same order.
.PP
Any other option goes to the stock
.B man
unchanged.
.SH FILES
.TP
.BI /opt/amix/man/ section / name
a package's page: plain troff with the
.B \-man
macros. A page that is only the line
.BI ".so " path
shows the page at
.I path
(an alias).
.TP
.BI /opt/amix/man/whatis.d/ package
the index lines of one package, in the stock
.I whatis
format:
.br
.BI "    " name ( section ) "     names \- description"
.TP
.BI /var/opt/amix/catman/ section / name
formatted pages kept to show them faster. Only a user who can write there
(root) keeps them; a page is formatted again when its source is newer. The
stock cache,
.BR /usr/catman ,
is never written for a package's page.
.TP
.B /usr/bin/man
the stock command, which this one calls; it is never changed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PAGER
the pager for terminal output.
.TP
.B MANPATH
passed to the stock
.B man
as it is, unless it points into
.BR /opt/amix ;
then it is dropped, with
.BR CATPATH ,
so that the stock
.B man
never caches a package's page in
.BR /usr/catman .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR more (1),
.BR eqn (1),
.BR nroff (1),
.BR tbl (1)
.SH NOTES
This command is installed as
.BR /usr/amix/bin/man .
.B /usr/amix/bin
comes before
.B /usr/bin
on the login
.BR PATH ;
it holds only commands like this one, which pass every request they do not
handle to the stock command of the same name.
